#%MACE-BASIS-LIBRARY 1
#%family full.basis.triplezeta.rev2022
#%description Opt-in update of full.basis.triplezeta (menu option 4, external_basis_family
#%description "tz-rev2022"). Rb-Mo and Ru-I use X_POB_TZVP_rev2 (Laun & Bredow, J. Comput.
#%description Chem. 2022, 43, 839) and La-Lu use X_pob_TZVP_rev2 (Seidler, Laun & Bredow,
#%description J. Comput. Chem. 2023) in place of pob-TZVP 2018 and ERD small-core 2017. Tc keeps
#%description the ERD 2017 all-electron record (the site has no Tc_POB_TZVP_rev2); every other
#%description record is byte-identical to full.basis.triplezeta.
#%description Core treatment: Rb-I keep the same INPUT ECP as pob-TZVP 2018 (same ZNUC). Ce-Lu
#%description use a 28-electron core with 4f in the valence (ZNUC = Z - 28), the same core size
#%description as the ERD small-core records. La differs: ZNUC = 11, a 46-electron core, where
#%description ERD has ZNUC = 29 - each La atom carries 18 fewer electrons than with
#%description full.basis.triplezeta, which shows in the Mulliken NO. OF ELECTRONS.
#%record 1 bytes=264
#%  source H_pob_TZVP_rev2
#%  reference D. Vilela Oliveira, M. F. Peintinger, J. Laun, T. Bredow, J. Comput. Chem. 40 (2019) 2364-2376
#%  doi 10.1002/jcc.26013
#%  url https://www.crystal.unito.it/Basis_Sets/hydrogen.html#H_pob_TZVP_rev2
#%  provenance exact numeric match to H_pob_TZVP_rev2 on crystal.unito.it (retrieved 2026-10-01)
